# OpenRouter API Key Configuration
# =================================
#
# Get your key from: https://openrouter.ai (sign up free, no card required)
#
# Steps:
# 1. Sign up for a free account at https://openrouter.ai
# 2. Open the OpenRouter dashboard and click "Keys"
# 3. Create a new key (looks like sk-or-v1-xxxxx)
# 4. Rename this file to .env
# 5. Replace the placeholder below with your actual API key

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your_api_key_here

# Two examples (13 code execution, 14 reasoning) call Groq directly for its
# native code-interpreter tool + prompt caching. Sign up free at
# https://console.groq.com to get this key.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your_api_key_here

# Notes:
# - Keep these keys secret! Never commit .env to version control
# - The .gitignore file should already exclude .env
# - For bash/curl examples: export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="your_key_here"
# - For Node.js: Use dotenv package or export to environment
# - For Python: Use python-dotenv or export to environment
# - For Go: Use godotenv or export to environment
# - For Arduino: Edit the API key directly in the .ino file
# - OpenRouter's free tier covers chat, vision, safety, prompt guard, tool
#   use, web search, transcription, and text-to-speech across this repo -
#   no whitelist, no proxy, direct connection to the provider
